Phase 5's real scope, corrected against this session's own 34-worker
audit rather than the doc's stale original line (see the plan doc's
latest entry): the doc names "leak-map, win-back, pile-on's remainder,
the Cold Open pipeline, and the Whop workers" as Phase 5 targets, but
14 of the 15 Whop Agent workers are confirmed zero-config and
explicitly flagged as workers that "should never get a setup flow, only
a toggle" — building Dossier UI for them would contradict this exact
doc's own finding. Real Phase 5 scope: leak-map, win-back, pile-on,
voice-capture, source-connect, send-connect, daily-send. (The 15th Whop
worker, whop-refund-dispute-velocity, needs schema migrations before
any UI is possible — that's Phase 6, not Phase 5.)

Pile-On chosen first because it's not a blank slate: Phase 2 already
tiered its fields and built its capability map (SMS Follow-ups,
Ad-Cohort Sync) in the "Encode Phase 2's field-risk tiers" commit, and
worker-capability-status.ts already has a filledKeysForPileOn reader
from Phase 3 slice 1 — none of that backend work has any UI consuming
it yet. This slice closes exactly that gap: wires the existing,
already-generic WorkerCapabilityMatrix component (its own API route
dispatches by workerId with no hardcoded worker list — confirmed by
reading it, not assumed) into pile-on-config-form.tsx, the same
one-line pattern already proven three times this session for
rep-onboarding/pre-call-read/icp-lock. Read-only, additive, above the
existing SMS/ad-data dropdowns — the existing save/enable logic is
completely untouched.

