First Cold Open pipeline worker on the corrected Phase 5 scope. Unlike
Pile-On (which already had Phase 2 data from earlier this session),
Voice Capture had none — this slice builds both layers from scratch,
same order Phase 2 originally went through for the top-5 workers.

Tiered against checkVoiceCapture's real gate logic, not the registry's
field list alone (Phase 2's own rule: tier must match what the real
checker actually blocks on, never silently diverge): checkVoiceCapture
blocks on exactly voiceProfile ("mirrors runVoiceCapture's own guard")
— subjectVariants and bodyVariantPools are registry-listed but not
actually gate-checked at all today. Tiered voiceProfile as blocking,
the other two as deferrable (bundled with whichever downstream worker
actually needs them — Pile-On's sequence for subject variants, Daily
Send's upload copyMode for body variant pools — rather than blocking
Voice Capture itself for fields it doesn't need to Arm).

