Fourth Cold Open pipeline worker on the corrected Phase 5 scope.

checkSendConnect blocks on sendPlatform alone ("mirrors runSendConnect's
own guard"). Tiered sendPlatform as blocking; sendPlatformCredential and
campaignMap as deferrable (neither independently checked by the gate,
same honest-gap shape already named for Source Connect's leadSourceCredential/
csvMapping); autoPushIcps as hidden-default, since it genuinely has a
real, safe, documented default (empty = nothing auto-pushed, everything
held for review) and was the field the full 34-worker audit found
completely undisclosed in this registry.

Caught and fixed a real mistake before verifying: first pass wrote
`kind: "hidden-default"` on autoPushIcps instead of `tier:
"hidden-default"` — kind and tier are two different fields on
WorkerConfigField (kind is "ask"/"secret"/etc, tier is the Phase 2 risk
tier), and tsc caught the type mismatch immediately. Fixed to `kind:
"ask", tier: "hidden-default"` before re-verifying.

WORKER_CAPABILITIES gets "Sending Configured", gating on sendPlatform
alone. filledKeysForSendConnect reads getColdOpenConfig's sendPlatform/
campaignMap/autoPushIcps directly, plus hasCredential(engagementId,
`cold_open_${platform}`) for sendPlatformCredential — the exact same
provider-key convention send-connect-config-form.tsx's own CredentialRow
already uses.

Wired WorkerCapabilityMatrix into send-connect-config-form.tsx —
read-only, additive, existing load/save logic untouched.

